---
id: org.dxos.plugin.space.object-share
name: Object share links
version: 0.1.0
---

Share one Composer object as you share a document in Google Docs. Each object has a **Share** button. The button opens a dialog, and **Copy link** makes a URL. The URL opens that object.

A browser with no identity gets an identity immediately. A guest that is not a member joins the space in the background. The guest replicates only the shared object and the objects that it needs, not the full space.

While the guest joins, the plank of the object waits for the space. EDGE can give the documents of the shared objects in one HTTP request, before the guest has an identity. A later change will open the client from these documents, as a boot cache (see [D-23]).

The feature has four parts:

- plugin-space (`org.dxos.plugin.space`, [F-2] there) owns the dialog, the link and the link handler.
- The client SDK sends the scope through the join.
- The ECHO host enforces the scope, and it answers queries before the index reads the documents.
- The db-service of EDGE serves the documents of the shared objects.

## Extensions

This document uses the extension dialects that follow. The Appendix defines each extension, or its URI identifies it.

| Term       | URI                         |
